Package: ristools
Title: Faithful Reading and Writing of RIS and BibTeX Bibliographic Files
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R:
    person("Mark", "Engelbert", email = "mengelbert@3ieimpact.org",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Reads and writes RIS and BibTeX bibliographic files without the
    data loss that affects several existing implementations. A RIS file becomes
    a data frame whose columns are the file's own tags, so it can be inspected,
    edited and written back with nothing renamed, merged or reordered. Multiple
    values in a single field (authors, keywords, JEL descriptors, ISSNs) are
    joined with a delimiter that cannot occur in bibliographic text, making the
    conversion reversible. Also handles byte order marks, detects file encoding,
    and preserves trailing punctuation in titles and tags containing digits.
    OpenAlex works can be read from JSON into the same flat data frame and
    written out as RIS.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Imports:
    jsonlite,
    stats
